From: U2W build
Subject: [PATCH] aacenc: accept AACENC_BITRATEMODE 8 for LD/ELD again

AACENC_BITRATEMODE 8 ("LD/ELD full bitreservoir for packet based
transmission") is still documented in aacenc_lib.h and still accepted by
aacEncoder_SetParam, but since 0.1.5 FDKaacEnc_AdjustEncSettings no longer
maps it to CBR, so the following check rejects it and the first
aacEncEncode(NULL, ...) fails with AACENC_INVALID_CONFIG (0x23).

AppleCarPlay configures its ELD encoder with exactly this mode (AOT 39,
SBR off, TT_MP4_RAW, granule 480, BITRATEMODE 8, no AACENC_BITRATE); with
stock 0.1.5/0.1.6 the CarPlay ELD (telephony/Siri uplink) encoder cannot be
created.  Restore the 0.1.4 semantics: CBR (bitrateMode 0, default bitrate
from rate/channels) with the full bit reservoir (bitreservoir -1, i.e.
maxBitres in FDKaacEnc_Initialize), instead of the reduced LD reservoir used
for mode 0.  With this patch the encoder yields the same ASC, bitrate and
frame count as the vendor 0.1.4 library for that parameter set.

--- a/libAACenc/src/aacenc_lib.cpp
+++ b/libAACenc/src/aacenc_lib.cpp
@@ -824,6 +824,11 @@
             hAacConfig->bitreservoir = bitreservoir & ~7; /* align to bytes */
           }
         }
+        if (config->userBitrateMode==8) {
+          /* Documented LD/ELD mode 8 (0.1.4): CBR with full bitreservoir. */
+          hAacConfig->bitrateMode = 0;
+          hAacConfig->bitreservoir = -1;
+        }
         if (hAacConfig->bitrateMode!=0) {
           return AACENC_INVALID_CONFIG;
         }
